From f01ae14c9b95338efae4e2ac2d62703bc873d178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frans Kaashoek <kaashoek@mit.edu>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:45:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wal: cut in SaveSnapshot once the tail passes
 SegmentSizeBytes, as Save does

SaveSnapshot appended its record to the tail and synced, but never cut.
The server saves a snapshot record from its apply thread once per applied
batch past SnapshotCount, and raft hands a commit backlog out over Readys
whose hard state and entries are empty (whose Save writes nothing, so no
cut), so the snapshot records between two entry-writing Saves grow one
tail file without bound, up to the file-size limit (EFBIG, and the apply
thread panics). SaveSnapshot now checks the tail's offset after the record
and cuts as Save does (cut syncs the old tail first). TestSaveSnapshotCuts
fails before the change (one file) and passes after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 server/storage/wal/savesnapshot_cut_test.go | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++
 server/storage/wal/wal.go                   | 13 +++-
 2 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 server/storage/wal/savesnapshot_cut_test.go

diff --git a/server/storage/wal/savesnapshot_cut_test.go b/server/storage/wal/savesnapshot_cut_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..287570944
--- /dev/null
+++ b/server/storage/wal/savesnapshot_cut_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
